  "parens_note": "Many entries list both `\"right\"` and `\"right>\"`. CPython's AST has no parenthesised-expression node -- `x = (y)` gives `Assign.value = y` -- so its child can sit one or more levels inside ours. The containment form is the true claim wherever parentheses are legal, and it still says the child is under the right FIELD, which is the part that matters."
